From 2cdd4e9d25f00c49112ea9949a54ddae9f470006 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini Mainline Experiment <gemini-mainline@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 09:59:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 120/120] i2c: mediatek: add fixed Fermi topology fingerprint

Quasar proved that the ordinary MT6797 iDVFS controller policy can perform
the fixed legacy-interface reads twice through the native FIFO path while
preserving the handoff, initialization, transfer, IRQ, and DMA invariants.
The next discriminator must retain that exact transport contract while
reading the legacy DA9213/14/15 topology and active voltage controls.

Add a compile-time-exclusive Fermi diagnostic derived from Quasar.  Its
root-only one-shot endpoint accepts only "run\n" and performs two fixed
passes over 0x69:{05,06,47} followed by 0x68:{d3,5e,d9,da}.  Require the
known d9,d0,c0 interface tuple, require the low three bits of d3 to be 05,
and require d3,5e,d9,da to remain stable across the two passes.  Reject a
sample that still equals its distinct receive prefill before interpreting
any unknown control value.

Keep every Quasar controller and counter invariant, including the childless
adapter and ready-handoff gates, zero initial transfer counters, native
packed 0x0101 WRRD lengths, FIFO completion, completion-only IRQs, one then
zero FIFO bytes, zero APDMA state, no hardware reinitialization, and exact
14/0/14/14 transfer/DMA/start/IRQ counters.  Increase only the fixed result
buffer so all fourteen complete snapshots fit without truncation.

The endpoint exposes no configurable address, register, length, data, mode,
retry, or reset input.  It performs no PAGE_CON or data-register write and
provides no I2C client or regulator.  It requests neither Cortex-A72.

